{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And he does not return to his heart.</b> An allusion to the intellect, which is the principal thing." "Mem with a vav in <b>bemo</b> is added like the word <i>kemo</i> (Psalms 58:10)." "<b>ve-yataro.</b> That which remains." "<b>le-val.</b> It has no [other] equivalent. Some say: to carve or to form. R. Moses the Cohen said that it is like <i>ki-vul harim</i> (Job 40:20), and the meaning is vegetation."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {3 "The phrase 'אין רע לו' literally means 'it has no evil to it'; rendered here as 'no equivalent' following Ibn Ezra's usage elsewhere, though the expression is unusual in this context."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:01.113360416Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}